<section class="section reveal" id="patterns">
  <span class="section-label">Patterns</span>
  <h2>Key Patterns and Best Practices</h2>

  <p>The most successful multi-tenant ai platforms implementations follow proven patterns. These patterns emerge from experience: failures, lessons learned, and incremental refinement.</p>

  <p><strong>Pattern 1: Design for Failure</strong> — Assume components will fail. Design systems that gracefully degrade rather than crash. Use circuit breakers, timeouts, and fallbacks.</p>

  <p><strong>Pattern 2: Instrument Everything</strong> — You cannot manage what you cannot measure. Instrument your code from day one. Make observability a first-class design concern.</p>

  <p><strong>Pattern 3: Automate Routine Tasks</strong> — Manual processes don't scale and introduce human error. Automate deployment, monitoring, alerting, and common remediation steps.</p>

  <p><strong>Pattern 4: Version and Iterate</strong> — Version your models, configurations, and infrastructure as code. Treat everything as deployable artifacts with clear versions and rollback capability.</p>

